1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,733
A policy changed: heavy courier deliveries with a loading dock no longer need unloading assistance.

2
00:00:06,733 --> 00:00:09,000
Which form questions must change?

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,800
FormRehearsal compares the old and amended interpretations after separate, explicit approvals.

4
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:22,000
These example rules are authored; both approvals here are agent-simulated.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:33,700
For this heavy courier request with a dock, the amended interpretation hides both questions; the original form shows them.

6
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:38,000
The explorer can inspect other declared requests.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,033
Compare the neighboring request without a dock.

8
00:00:41,033 --> 00:00:42,767
Both questions remain visible.

9
00:00:42,767 --> 00:00:48,000
Only the dock answer differs, making the policy exception easy to inspect.

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,167
Two of sixteen declared combinations change.

11
00:00:51,167 --> 00:00:54,300
Urgency does not affect this exception.

12
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:58,000
Access-instructions visibility stays unknown in every combination.

13
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,267
The unresolved clause says “special arrangements”.

14
00:01:01,267 --> 00:01:10,000
The policy owner must decide when access instructions should appear, and whether that needs another input.

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,600
Load the authored example revision.

16
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:17,800
It supplies two visibility edits and fills the editor only.

17
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:23,000
Inspect those edits, then explicitly recheck against the amended approval.

18
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:30,900
The fresh result reports no discrepancies across five covered slots and sixteen combinations.

19
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:37,000
One slot remains unchecked, so this is a partial check.

20
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,400
Download the exact checked form and its result.

21
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:48,000
Editing, even then reverting, disables those downloads until a fresh check completes.

22
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,600
The developer can take the exact checked revision forward.

23
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:55,200
The policy owner has a grounded question to resolve.

24
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:58,000
Both remain tied to their review scope.
